    In JDBC interpreter setting add following properties&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ol&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;zeppelin.jdbc.auth.type = KERBEROS&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;zeppelin.jdbc.principal = principal value&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;zeppelin.jdbc.keytab.location = keytab location&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;enable shiro authentication via shiro.ini&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;    Now try and run any of hive&apos;s query (say show tables) it should return with valid results/errors depending on user permission.&lt;/p&gt;

